<title>GERMANY: One in five German firms readying for EMU - DIHT.</title>
<headline>One in five German firms readying for EMU - DIHT.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Every fifth German company has started to prepare for the introduction of the euro, according to a survey conducted by the DIHT economic research institute.</p>
<p>The DIHT said almost two-thirds of firms it polled expected European monetary union to start on time in January 1, 1999, up sharply from previous surveys.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
